      "writtenOn": "2025-04-25T20:53:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Todd,\nWe\u0027re only turning on ARCH specific configs (CONFIG_ARCH_BCM, CONFIG_ARCH_BRCMSTB) that enable the framework to run BRCMSTB SOCs in the kernel. The rest of the changes are actually disabling BRCMSTB drivers as builtin modules so they can be run as loadable vendor modules. We have made similar submissions to android14-6.1 in the past.\nThanks.",
      "parentUuid": "f268ff51_946e0ab9",
      "revId": "701f180518c25508ccddb133cb4dd4c7c0c027b8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
